    "passives": {
      "HitTargetPassiveAWhiteSnakeGirlDark": {
        "id": "HitTargetPassiveAWhiteSnakeGirlDark",
        "found": true,
        "localization": {
          "name": "Black-Hearted",
          "description": "This unit cannot be defeated by damage from Poison status effects, and cannot be sent to the reinforcements from the battlefield.\n\nThis unit has 50% damage reduction from attacks, and reduces the amount of any stun effects against the unit by 50TU.\n\nThis unit's attacks heal this unit for 100% of total damage dealt, ignore damage reduction effects, and any effects of non-boss enemies that would prevent targets from being defeated.\n\nEach time this unit damages any number of non-conjured units with an attack, this unit will immediately get the next turn. If this triggers 3 times within 50TU, this effect cannot trigger again until 50TU advances. This effect can trigger again against the same unit. Effects that influence TU order may interrupt the extra turn (e.g. Stuns targeting the lowest TU target)."
        }
      },
      "BecomeDeathPassiveAWhiteSnakeGirlDark": {
        "id": "BecomeDeathPassiveAWhiteSnakeGirlDark",
        "found": true,
        "localization": {
          "name": "Snake Formation",
          "description": "This unit enters battle with Super Stealth, and an Instant Death Ward.\n\nIf this unit would be defeated by an enemy attack or a status effect while having more than 1 HP, it instead survives with 1 HP.\n\nWhenever this unit gets the turn, if this unit's Active Skills are not disabled, this unit can't have its Active Skills disabled until the end of its turn.\n\nEach time this unit takes damage from an attack and survives until after the end of the turn, this unit will be Purified, and heal for 50% of its max HP.\n\nThis unit has a 20% chance to grant a random enemy an Ambush Counter whenever this unit or another unit (ally or enemy) enters the battlefield from reinforcements. This chance is increased by 20% per Awakening, up to 100% chance if this unit has 4 Awakenings.\n\nWhen a unit with an Ambush Counter takes a turn, and survives until after the end of the turn, 2 random units on their opposing team will be given the next turns by reducing their current TU, then the Ambush Counter is removed. These TU reductions may trigger before or after other effects that adjust the turn order. Ambush counters are not a status effect. Ambush counters cannot stack, cannot apply to boss units, and cannot be purified. An ambush counter is removed from a unit that is defeated or leaves the battlefield."
        }
      },
